abstract: >-
  A reference model and implemented wire mechanisms for the "existence layer" beneath
  agent protocols such as MCP and A2A: who an agent is, which human answers for it, what it
  may do while unsupervised, whether it is alive, and how its actions are proven afterwards.
  Two interoperating implementations (Node, Python), deterministic test vectors, and a
  two-process demonstration accompany the specification.
